Description: efi/peimage: only register loader when shim loader protocol absent
 No CVE: a functional fix, needed with shim 16.
 .
 shim 16 provides an image loader protocol. GRUB uses it and registers it as
 the EFI loader override (grub-core/kern/efi/sb.c, at EFI init). Ubuntu's
 peimage module (debian/patches/secure-boot/efi-peimage.patch) then also
 registered its own loader in GRUB_MOD_INIT, which fails and prints
 "error: trying to register different loader." on every Secure Boot boot
 with shim 16 (Debian's shim 16.1, which BeastBoot ships).
 .
 With this change peimage registers its loader only when shim offers no image
 loader protocol (shim 15.x: peimage keeps loading kernels, verified through
 shim_lock, as before), and GRUB_MOD_FINI unregisters it only if it was
 registered. Which loader runs is unchanged: with shim 16 it was already
 shim's (the second registration failed); only the error goes away. No
 signature check or lockdown decision is touched.
 .
 Why we carry it: Ubuntu's grub2 2.14-2ubuntu3 lacks it. It is Debian's fix,
 salsa grub-team/grub commit 8719ef8a523f2a89aeff1b86f5e14c3bba7a7d11
 (2026-06-23, Mate Kukri), which changes efi-peimage.patch itself; here the
 same change is applied to the patched source (grub-core/loader/efi/peimage.c
 of Ubuntu 2.14-2ubuntu3, same code as Debian's). build/grub/security-fixes.json
 checks on every build that it is present (and absent from Ubuntu's tree
 alone). It changes no SBAT generation (grub.peimage stays as Ubuntu has it).
Origin: vendor, https://salsa.debian.org/grub-team/grub/-/commit/8719ef8a523f2a89aeff1b86f5e14c3bba7a7d11
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-25
---
diff --git a/grub-core/loader/efi/peimage.c b/grub-core/loader/efi/peimage.c
--- a/grub-core/loader/efi/peimage.c
+++ b/grub-core/loader/efi/peimage.c
@@ -910,13 +910,28 @@
   .unload_image = do_unload_image,
 };
 
+static int registered;
+
 GRUB_MOD_INIT (peimage)
 {
-  grub_efi_register_loader (&peimage_loader);
+  static grub_guid_t shim_loader_guid = GRUB_EFI_SHIM_IMAGE_LOADER_GUID;
+
   my_mod = mod;
+
+  /*
+   * When shim provides its own image loader protocol grub uses that (see
+   * grub-core/kern/efi/sb.c), which registers it as the override loader. Do
+   * not register a second one.
+   */
+  if (grub_efi_locate_protocol (&shim_loader_guid, 0) != NULL)
+    return;
+
+  grub_efi_register_loader (&peimage_loader);
+  registered = 1;
 }
 
 GRUB_MOD_FINI (peimage)
 {
-  grub_efi_unregister_loader (&peimage_loader);
+  if (registered)
+    grub_efi_unregister_loader (&peimage_loader);
 }
